Having finished my explore mode slash'em game (the endgame is really 
easy for lawfuls - you don't even have to kill the riders yourself, if 
you have sacrificed enough to get some planetar pets; in fact, they will 
even kill all demon lords for you, except Demogorgon), I decided to 
check out how to kill One-eyed Sam, since sometimes this might be necessary.

My first strategy worked as anticipated.  I went to the entrance, read a 
blessed scroll of earth to get some blocking boulders between Sam and 
myself (actually, Sam was a Samantha, swinging *her* sword named 
Thiefbane).  However, Sam stood at a knight's distance which was not 
good for attacking him with missiles.  So I took out my pick axe to 
remove the boulders to my left and right to be able to shoot diagonally. 
  This turned out unnecessary, because the very moment I took out the 
pick axe, Sam uttered some insult and moved in front of the entrance 
door to block me from entering.  Then I wielded my +4 assault rifle, 
quivered some 100 +6 bullet and started shooting at her.  There were up 
to six bullets shot in one round.  After two rounds, Sam died for the 
first time, was saved by her amulet of life saving only to die after 
three more rounds...  Therefore, fire arms work nicely, if one has 
enough or sufficiently highly enchanted bullets.

The second strategy that I tried was to get a powerful pet into the 
shop.  Since the most powerful pets I know of so far are planetars, I 
wished for a  blessed figurine of a planetar.  The first attempt gave me 
only a peaceful planetar and when I tried to tame it by a scroll of 
taming, it got angry, so I had to kill it.  During this fight, I was hit 
several times by the planetar, despite an AC of -44.  My next blessed 
figurine of a planetar did produce a tame planetar and since his level 
was higher than that of Sam, he started attacking him with his long 
sword.  But in spite of the fact that Sam's AC was only -27, *all* the 
attacks of my planetar were blocked by Sam's armor.  Even after 10 or so 
turns, Sam was still at 155 (155) hit points.  So this strategy does not 
work.  But why doesn't it?  Why can a planetar easlily take hit points 
away from a character with AC -44 but does not succeed with Sam who had 
only an AC of -27?  Is there a difference in evaluating AC effects for 
monsters and the player?  By the way, not even once did Sam retaliate...

Another idea I have not yet checked is a purple worm.  It would probably 
not attack Sam, its level being too low.  However, if I put on a ring of 
conflict while it is close to Sam, it might swallow him and instakill 
him - if his AC does not prevent that either.  Also, I am not sure about 
  getting his equipment then.  (Thiefbane is really a two edged weapon. 
If you hit a level drain resistant monster with it you had better wear 
an amulet of drain resistance...  But its beheading feature is nice.)
